WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.013
Kamalbaddh Navkar Dhyan

00:00:03.013 --> 00:00:05.850
The worship of the Navkar Mantra

00:00:05.850 --> 00:00:08.422
is a great spiritual practice. 

00:00:08.422 --> 00:00:11.501
The Navkar Mantra destroys all sins 

00:00:11.853 --> 00:00:15.350
and leads to the attainment of a pure self. 

00:00:15.790 --> 00:00:17.711
Through the worship of the Navkar Mantra,

00:00:17.711 --> 00:00:19.708
sins are eradicated,

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:22.129
suffering is dispelled,

00:00:22.129 --> 00:00:25.182
and auspiciousness begins.

00:00:26.657 --> 00:00:31.171
Now, we will recite the Navkar Mantra
 in the form of a lotus.

00:00:31.893 --> 00:00:34.840
Sit in a Sukhashan position on Aasan.

00:00:35.676 --> 00:00:39.180
Stay as steady as possible

00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:41.990
and try to sit upright.

00:00:43.289 --> 00:00:47.050
Place your palms on your knees.

00:00:48.855 --> 00:00:51.754
Join your thumbs and your first finger, 

00:00:51.754 --> 00:00:54.304
that is index finger,

00:00:56.113 --> 00:00:59.126
letting the other three fingers remain straight. 

00:01:00.095 --> 00:01:02.535
This is known as the Gyan Mudra.

00:01:04.186 --> 00:01:08.057
Now, gently close your eyes.

00:01:09.422 --> 00:01:11.627
Relax your body.

00:01:12.639 --> 00:01:16.133
Focus your complete attention on your breath.

00:01:17.938 --> 00:01:20.554
Now, inhale slowly...

00:01:24.891 --> 00:01:27.727
and exhale slowly...

00:01:33.855 --> 00:01:37.154
Repeat this process five times.

00:01:39.113 --> 00:01:41.882
Focus your attention on your breath.
 

00:01:42.520 --> 00:01:45.511
Now, inhale slowly...

00:01:53.568 --> 00:01:57.145
and exhale slowly...

00:02:04.616 --> 00:02:06.616
Inhale

00:02:11.107 --> 00:02:13.107
Exhale

00:02:19.021 --> 00:02:21.021
Inhale

00:02:26.810 --> 00:02:28.810
Exhale

00:02:34.715 --> 00:02:36.715
Inhale

00:02:41.250 --> 00:02:43.250
Exhale

00:02:49.266 --> 00:02:53.085
First, in each petal

00:02:53.085 --> 00:02:56.164
 visualize one of the Navkar Mantra verses 

00:02:58.035 --> 00:03:03.956
Today, we need to meditate 
 on the eight - petaled lotus in our hearts

00:03:04.666 --> 00:03:09.098
 In the center, 
 'Namo Arihantanam,' 

00:03:09.590 --> 00:03:12.294
above it 'Namo Siddhanam,'

00:03:13.571 --> 00:03:16.738
to the right 'Namo Ayariyanam,'

00:03:17.486 --> 00:03:20.741
below 'Namo Uvajjhayanam,'

00:03:21.908 --> 00:03:25.647
to the left 'Namo Loe Savva Sahunam.'

00:03:25.647 --> 00:03:27.647
visualise

00:03:28.175 --> 00:03:32.068
Then, top right corner, 
 'Eso Panch Namukkaro,'

00:03:32.574 --> 00:03:35.000
 bottom right corner, 'Savva Pav - Panasano,'

00:03:35.440 --> 00:03:37.440
 bottom left corner, 'Mangala Nam Ch Savvesim,' 

00:03:37.940 --> 00:03:38.748
and top left corner

00:03:39.217 --> 00:03:41.355
'Padham Havai Mangalam.'

00:03:41.355 --> 00:03:43.355
visualise

00:03:44.544 --> 00:03:47.336
The phrase 'Namo Arihantanam,' 

00:03:47.864 --> 00:03:50.767
who is adorned with eight Pratiharyas in 
 the center

00:03:51.493 --> 00:03:54.704
It is to pay homage to the infinite 
 Arihanta Paramatma.

00:03:55.717 --> 00:03:57.246
the 24 Tirthankars of the past,

00:03:57.378 --> 00:03:59.082
present 24 Tirthankars,

00:03:59.434 --> 00:04:02.315
 and future 24 Tirthankars

00:04:02.557 --> 00:04:07.529
currently are in the Mahavidya Kshetra region.

00:04:07.859 --> 00:04:12.633
Even the 20 wandering Tirthankars 
 are also saluted.

00:04:13.337 --> 00:04:14.937
In this way beings,

00:04:14.937 --> 00:04:17.507
those in the past, present and future 

00:04:17.507 --> 00:04:21.410
Tirthankars are worshipped through this phrase.

00:04:22.563 --> 00:04:24.387
When reciting this phrase,

00:04:24.387 --> 00:04:26.901
imagine a white colour

00:04:27.980 --> 00:04:30.000
because the Arihant Paramatma 

00:04:30.604 --> 00:04:32.667
 is an ocean of infinite compassion,

00:04:32.667 --> 00:04:34.805
and that compassion

00:04:34.805 --> 00:04:36.821
is continuously showering upon us.

00:04:37.393 --> 00:04:39.530
The phrase 'Namo Siddhanam'

00:04:39.530 --> 00:04:42.514
is to worship to the infinite Siddha Paramatma.

00:04:43.372 --> 00:04:46.039
 Siddha Bhagwan of the past,

00:04:46.039 --> 00:04:49.555
in the present,the Mahavidyakshetra

00:04:49.555 --> 00:04:51.995
The Atma attaining Moksh

00:04:51.995 --> 00:04:56.702
and the future Siddha Bhagwans

00:04:56.702 --> 00:04:59.164
are also worshipped through this phrase

00:05:00.177 --> 00:05:01.654
When reciting this phrase,

00:05:01.654 --> 00:05:04.285
imagine a red colour.

00:05:05.000 --> 00:05:09.715
Gold also becomes pure 
 and red when subjected to fire,

00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:13.333
Similarly, the Siddha Bhagwan has become 
 pure and radiant

00:05:13.333 --> 00:05:16.346
 through the purification of their karmas.

00:05:17.865 --> 00:05:20.503
The phrase 'Namo Aayariyanam'

00:05:20.503 --> 00:05:24.022
is a salutation to the infinite Acharya Bhagwants

00:05:24.522 --> 00:05:27.444
In the image, infinite Acharya Bhagwants

00:05:27.444 --> 00:05:29.153
are imparting the Lord's teachings to

00:05:29.153 --> 00:05:32.582
the entire congregation through their discourses.

00:05:33.886 --> 00:05:39.892
Acharya Bhagwants of the past, present, and future

00:05:39.892 --> 00:05:42.312
are worshipped through this phrase.

00:05:42.862 --> 00:05:47.085
When reciting this phrase, 
 imagine a yellow colour. 

00:05:48.369 --> 00:05:50.633
Acharyas are like saffron-colored lions,

00:05:51.373 --> 00:05:53.688
spreading the rays of knowledge

00:05:53.688 --> 00:05:55.773
throughout the world,

00:05:56.059 --> 00:05:59.116
which is why their colour is envisioned as yellow.

00:05:59.622 --> 00:06:02.613
The phrase 'Namo Uvajjyanam'

00:06:02.613 --> 00:06:07.166
is a salutation to the infinite Upadhyaya Bhagwants.

00:06:07.735 --> 00:06:10.408
In the picture, infinite Upadhyaya Bhagwants

00:06:10.408 --> 00:06:13.609
are imparting teachings to all their disciples.

00:06:13.609 --> 00:06:16.715
Upadhyaya Bhagwants of the past, present, and future

00:06:16.715 --> 00:06:19.883
who are engaged in imparting knowledge,

00:06:19.883 --> 00:06:22.545
are worshipped through this phrase.

00:06:23.007 --> 00:06:27.913
When reciting this phrase, 
 imagine a green colour.

00:06:27.913 --> 00:06:32.665
Upadhyayas are like the shade of a tree, 

00:06:32.665 --> 00:06:33.994
knowledge to all living beings,

00:06:33.994 --> 00:06:36.734
which is why their colour is envisioned as green.

00:06:36.734 --> 00:06:40.000
The phrase 'Namo - Loe - Savvasaahunm'

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:44.289
is to worship to the infinite Sadhu-Sadhvi Bhagwants.

00:06:44.839 --> 00:06:47.596
In the image, infinite Sadhu Bhagwants

00:06:47.596 --> 00:06:50.489
are engaged in practices such as 
 tapas and kaushagga.

00:06:50.489 --> 00:06:51.631
Past,

00:06:51.631 --> 00:06:52.971
future,

00:06:52.971 --> 00:07:01.839
And present Sadhu - Sadhvi Bhagwants 
 are also worshipped through this phrase.

00:07:01.839 --> 00:07:04.543
Wandering in the land of Bharat - Kshetra, 

00:07:04.543 --> 00:07:07.215
 there are thousands of Sadhu - Sadhvijis, 

00:07:07.215 --> 00:07:10.352
while in the Mahavidyakshetra region, 

00:07:10.352 --> 00:07:12.248
there are 200 billion Sadhus

00:07:12.248 --> 00:07:14.774
and 200 billion Sadhvijis.

00:07:14.774 --> 00:07:19.510
 are worshipped through this phrase.

00:07:19.510 --> 00:07:21.466
When reciting this phrase,

00:07:21.466 --> 00:07:24.408
imagine a black colour.

00:07:24.408 --> 00:07:28.254
Just as the colour black is not affected 
 by other colours,

00:07:28.254 --> 00:07:31.918
Sadhu Bhagwants are not affected

00:07:31.918 --> 00:07:34.789
by attachment or aversion,

00:07:34.789 --> 00:07:37.560
which is why their colour is envisioned as black.

00:07:38.176 --> 00:07:41.052
While reciting the remaining four phrases,

00:07:41.052 --> 00:07:44.535
imagine a white colour

00:07:45.482 --> 00:07:49.551
Now, we will recite 
 the Navkar Mantra, three times.

00:07:50.233 --> 00:07:56.790
NAMO ARIHANTANAM

00:07:58.415 --> 00:08:04.245
NAMO SIDDHANAM

00:08:05.560 --> 00:08:11.133
NAMO AYARIYANAM

00:08:12.926 --> 00:08:18.580
NAMO UVAJJHAYANAM

00:08:19.703 --> 00:08:26.279
NAMO LOE SAVVASAHUNAM

00:08:27.731 --> 00:08:33.913
ESO PANCH NAMOKKARO

00:08:35.476 --> 00:08:41.596
SAVVA PAVA PPANASANO

00:08:42.063 --> 00:08:48.116
MANGALANANCHA SAVVESIM

00:08:48.824 --> 00:08:54.900
PADHAMAM HAVEI MANGALAM

